message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Graphene oxide probe sorption explorer: interactive analysis of molecular-probe sorption on graphene oxide"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ulyanov
    given-names: Grigory
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/grulyanov/Graphene-Clusterization"
url: "https://graphene-clusterization.streamlit.app/"
keywords:
  - graphene oxide
  - sorption
  - molecular probes
  - Kamlet–Taft parameters
  - donor number
  - RANSAC
  - clustering
  - permutation test
  - Streamlit
abstract: >-
  Interactive web application (Streamlit) for analysing the sorption of molecular probes on
  graphene oxide. It reproduces the analysis notebook (k-means, hierarchical, spectral and
  DBSCAN clustering; sequential RANSAC correlations of sorption with Kamlet–Taft parameters,
  donor number, proton affinity and surface descriptors; RANSAC planes; collinearity
  diagnostics; nested leave-one-out PLS; conditional and full permutation tests) on an editable
  dataset, with substances and descriptors that can be added, edited and excluded. Russian
  (app.py) and English (app_en.py) interfaces. Code: MIT; data: CC BY 4.0.
